    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d706">

                <pb facs="0977" n="963" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg963"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.24/1715</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Chief of the China Division of the Foreign
                        Economic Administration</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">McCann</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Adviser to the Liberated Areas Division</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Moffat</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-23">April 23, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Moffat</hi>: The enclosed<anchor n="13a"
                        xml:id="d706-f1"/> covers the first specific request through Universal
                    Trading Corporation for used commercial industrial equipment to be purchased and
                    held for post war shipment.</p>
                <p>Universal Trading Corporation are as you know the Chinese Government cash
                    purchase agency in this country.</p>
                <p>We shall be interested in State Department’s opinion as to the desirability of
                    sponsoring this and similar requests. This is a commercial transaction—no
                    request is made for Lend-Lease aid.</p>
                <p>Were shipment desired at this time we would register objection on the grounds
                    that such material will only further congest warehousing facilities in
                    India.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">R. E. McCann</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
